# Generated run output: scored candidates, run JSON and the dashboards built
# from them. All reproducible with `python run.py`, and the dashboards are
# ~650K each, so they would dominate the diff of every run.
out/

# Downloaded PDB and mmCIF files: 116 MB across 108 structures, which is
# ~95% of everything on disk and none of it authored here. They are public
# data fetched by accession from files.rcsb.org, and the accessions ARE
# tracked -- data/catalog/ and data/targets/manifest.json record every id.
#
# To restore them after a fresh clone:
#     python scripts/fetch_data.py
#
# Everything else under data/ is deliberately committed, including the
# caches. data/lineage/expression.json and data/lineage/topology.json each
# carry a `fetched` date and a source string, and the whole discipline of
# this project is being able to say when a number was true and where it came
# from. Those files are small, and losing the record of what the Human
# Protein Atlas said on a given day would cost more than they take up.
data/structures/

